[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Document" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/core/document.gd" id="1_doc"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_doc")
id = &"d22_stage_record"
title = "Stilling well — gauge record"
byline = "Corps form, kept daily until 1994 and not since"
hand = 0
body = "RIDGEWATER LOCK & DAM
POOL STAGE, FEET ABOVE DATUM

The last page in the book is 1994 and the
readings stop mid-month, in Pfeiffer's hand.

11 MAR 94, 21.6 FT
12 MAR 94, 21.5 FT
14 MAR 94, 21.4 FT
15 MAR 94, 21.4 FT

Below that, in pencil, in a different hand,
one line per year and nothing else:

1995, 21.4 FT
1996, 21.3 FT
1997, 21.4 FT
1998, 21.4 FT

A pool held by a closed dam does not move.
That is what a closed dam is for.

FLOOD RESPONSE SEQUENCE HOLDS WHILE STAGE
EXCEEDS 30.0 FT. SEE OPERATING CARD."
